  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH services response for South Sudanese population in White Nile State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed CAFOD intervention will target 72,547 South Sudanese refugees in Alagaya, Dabat Bosin, Um Sangor, Jory, Kashafa and Elredeas camps, in White Nile state. As agreed through the WASH cluster in Kosti, CAFOD will provide the operation and maintenance of water distribution points in the camps and safe sanitation facilities  through the construction of gender sensitive communal bathing shower structures. The bathing shower superstructures will use Iron Zinc sheet and other materials including, gravel, bricks, slabs and steel items will be used for the sub-structure.  Latrine rehabilitation and emptying and protection from flooding will also be carried out.  These activities will be accompanied by hygiene promotion messaging, and general cleaning campaigns to improve the health and wellbeing of the refugees in the targeted camps.</narrative>
  </description>
